    {
      "title": "Core Workflow: groupby with agg",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Core Workflow: groupby with agg",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Keys, Column, Aggregation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Key(s)",
                    "sub": "groupby(['city','year'])",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Column",
                    "sub": "['sales']",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Aggregation",
                    "sub": ".mean()",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Two keys give a ==MultiIndex== result",
                "`as_index=False` keeps the keys as columns",
                "`.reset_index()` turns the keys back into columns"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Several Aggregations",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==list== on one column: columns are the function names",
                "==Named aggregation==: `name=(column, func)` gives clean names"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df.groupby('city')['sales'].agg(['sum','mean','count'])",
                "df.groupby('city').agg(total=('sales','sum'),",
                "    avg=('sales','mean'), n=('id','count'))"
              ],
              "note": "named form can mix columns"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Different functions per column",
              "text": "Use ==named aggregation==, one `name=(column, func)` keyword each."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Different functions per column?** Named aggregation, one keyword per output",
                "**Named aggregation?** `name=(column, func)`; the keyword becomes the column name",
                "**as_index=False?** Keys stay ordinary columns instead of the index"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "transform vs agg vs apply",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "transform vs agg vs apply",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Shape of the result",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "agg",
                "transform"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Output",
                  "one scalar per group",
                  "same length as df"
                ],
                [
                  "Rows",
                  "one per group",
                  "same as df"
                ],
                [
                  "Index",
                  "group keys",
                  "original index"
                ],
                [
                  "Assign back",
                  "needs a merge",
                  "directly as a column"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Transform examples",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Share of group total: ==transform== broadcasts the sum to every row"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df['pct'] = df['sales'] / df.groupby('city')['sales'].transform('sum')"
              ],
              "note": "each row's share of its city total"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Standardise per group: `transform(lambda s: (s - s.mean()) / s.std())`",
                "Group-wise fill: `transform(lambda s: s.fillna(s.mean()))`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**When transform, not agg?** When you need a per-row value to assign back as a column",
                "**Index guarantee?** Same length and original index as df, so it aligns",
                "**Why are built-in names faster?** `'sum'` runs optimized code; a lambda or apply runs Python per group"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Need a column back on df? ==transform==. Need a summary table? ==agg==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
